{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>Turn for yourselves.</b> I had said to bring you through the breadth of the land of Edom, along the north side, to enter the land — you spoiled it and caused delay for yourselves." "<b>Turn for yourselves.</b> Backward, and walk in the wilderness toward the Sea of Reeds — for the wilderness through which they were traveling, on the south side of Mount Seir, was interrupted between the Sea of Reeds and Mount Seir. Now continue toward the sea and go around Mount Seir along its entire south side, from west to east."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:35.403483946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}